# HIVE OPERATING FLOOR
## Unified Builder Manual

**Architecture rebuild brief + operating harness · one closed implement path**

PUBLIC-SHARE · FRAMEWORK PACK · NO ROOT REPOS REQUIRED

AdventureNLearn · AOS Control Plane

---

### DECISION / ASK

Recreate the base from this single record. Then attach your domain.
Worked examples are plug-ins, not the framework. Strip case chrome before sharing.
Success: another careful person rebuilds the base without inheriting private material.

**Edition U-1.2.0 · 8 September 2026 · Floor required · Civic packet optional**

HUMAN FINAL CALL REMAINS ABSOLUTE · NO PRIVATE CASE CONTENT · DUAL-TRACK

---

## 0 · What this is — and what it is not

This manual stands one operating floor on top of a language model: a written kernel, durable state, named seats, honesty labels, and a human final call. It merges two source records — a rebuild brief for the building, and a harness guide for the first session — so a stranger does not have to reconcile them.

This manual is a closed implement path: individualization sheet, kernel, folder skeleton, schemas, first-session paste, dry session, dual-track scrub, and pass/fail tests. This manual is **not** a consumer app, a downloadable computer OS, a dump of research, a license to copy private working documents, or an attack toolkit. Published “operator” names in older folders are process labels, not payloads. Skills without a kernel and a working document are only prompts.

### HARD TRUTH RULE

A human still decides what is true enough to share. Attention is not a truth signal. Software never crowns Supported. An honest open hole is better than a finished-looking fake board.

### Success criterion

Another careful person rebuilds the base from this written record, then attaches their own domain without inheriting someone else’s private material. Continuability is the test: hand the files and the latest artifact to a second person who was not in the chat. If they cannot continue, the system failed even if the chat was brilliant.

### Version honesty

A replicable guide that hides version lag is a false complete picture. If a step comes from a dated public file, name it. If a step is current practice that has not been published as a tagged release, mark it **Practice**. Do not launder Practice as a frozen public spec.

| Layer | Public record | This manual uses |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Architecture brief | Hive Brain rebuild brief, 7 Sep 2026. | Building, rooms, seed tree, rebuild recipe, schemas. |
| Harness guide | Operating Harness Builder Guide Ed. 1.0, 28 Aug 2026. | Individualization, seven laws, working document, Frame Audit, session-one, dual-track. |
| AOS-Public | Civic frameworks. Repository archived 14 Aug 2026. | Philosophy, scrubbing rules, Shatter as ancestor (cite once). Library attach only. |
| Sovereign Edition repo | User guide described 4-agent activation. Tree archived. | On-ramp pattern. Translate “4-agent” to BUILD / VERIFY / DOMAIN. |
| Live operator kernel | Not a single frozen public tag. | 3-role live seats + coordinator + human final call. Marked Practice. |
| Claim scoring | Evidence Gate + two-axis honesty kernel in both sources. | Both axes required. +1 only after the close rule. Software never mints Supported. |

**Tri-state on this pack:** operating laws as written in the two source briefs = Evidence. That a stranger will succeed = Inference. That ZIP-only with no working document works = Disputed by both sources.

