### Vocabulary map · translation only (one page, then stop)

Public language is the default everywhere else in this book. This table exists so a builder who saw older packs can translate. **Do not teach from the right-hand column. Do not print older ceremonial words on civic product screens, navigation, or footers.**

| Public word (use this) | If you saw older packs… | What it is |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Human / final call | Queen | Owns truth-enough-to-share and release. Not a seat file. |
| Coordinator | Keeper | Owns session order, spine, synthesis, host interface. |
| Implement / Build seat | Builder (BUILD) | Makes the artifact. Never mints Supported. Seat name BUILD is fine. |
| Verify seat | Guard (VERIFY) | First-paint, leak checklist, ship/no-ship. Verb = gate. File name = verify. |
| Label seat | Scout (DOMAIN) | Frame, claim list, card id, kicker, honesty strip. |
| Working document | Comb | Locked cells that survive chat reset. Living file: `WORKING.md`. |
| Primary records | Nectar | Commentary is not evidence. |
| Continuable artifact | Honey | Someone else can continue. |
| Frame Audit | Shatter / Layer-0 | Assumption audit before synthesis on high-stakes work. Shatter named once as ancestor in sources. |
| Polity Filter | Desk Layer-0 | Civic routing skill. Optional plug-in. Does not mint Supported. |
| Private floor | Harvest / collector / inbox | Fenced until a human promotes through Verify + OPSEC. |
| System / project | Colony | The operator’s named instance of this floor. Living identity file: `IDENTITY.md`. |
| Live seats / role set | Swarm (as metaphor) | Named roles on for this session. Not theater on public glass. |
| Session | Sitting | One bounded stretch of work. Dated export lives under `sessions/`. |

**After this page:** use the public word only. Never create a Scout seat or Guard seat in the seed tree. Seat file name for the fourth gate role is `verify`. The verb of that seat is **gate**. Do not write `seats/gate.md`.

**Alias note (older packs):** older packs used `COLONY.md` and `COMB.md`. Treat those names as aliases of `IDENTITY.md` and `WORKING.md`. Prefer the new names in every new file, template, and audit.

---

### How to use this book

1. Work in the printed order (§0 → §14).
2. Do not plug a real domain until the dry session is logged (§12 / §13).
3. The **floor is required** for every system. The **civic packet is optional** and attaches only when I-5 is civic glass / power-mapping.
4. Session-zero living files are `IDENTITY.md`, `KERNEL.md`, and `WORKING.md`.
5. `IDENTITY.md` stays operator-local. The share pack gets charter, kernel, refuses, empty templates — never a filled identity sheet, never private-floor material.
6. Start with the individualization inventory (§1). If I-2, I-3, I-9, or I-11 is blank, stop.

