## 01 · Individualization inventory — session zero

A copied system with someone else’s spine is costume. Before the first model session, fill every row into `IDENTITY.md`. If I-2 (spine), I-3 (final-call rule), I-9 (forbidden), or I-11 (first real task) is blank, **stop**. There is nothing to implement yet.

Do not put legal names, phones, home addresses, passwords, API keys, or live case identifiers in `IDENTITY.md` if it might be shared. Use stable codenames. `IDENTITY.md` is operator-local. The share pack receives charter / kernel / refuses extracted from it, not the identity sheet.

| ID | You must provide | Why the system needs it | Bad default |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| I-1 | System name (project name, not a legal name) | Every artifact and working doc needs a stable title. | Using another operator’s brand on public glass |
| I-2 | Mission spine — one sentence you will not bargain | Frame Audit and Verify need a spine to detect drift. | Copying a creed you do not hold |
| I-3 | Final-call rule — who has final call, and on what | Software must not auto-truth or auto-publish. | “The model decides when it’s done” |
| I-4 | Default target class: public-suite / pattern-lab / ops-only / archive | Stops lab chrome leaking onto public surfaces. | One pile for jokes and official findings |
| I-5 | First domain (one): research, writing, records, build/QA, civic glass, other | Week-3 module must attach to real work. Civic packet attaches only if this row is civic glass. | Installing every published skill first |
| I-6 | Host model and how you start a session | Activation text has to match the host. | Assuming a private machine layout |
| I-7 | Memory substrate: files, repo, chat-only, other | The working document has to live somewhere outside one window. | Trusting the chat to remember |
| I-8 | Shared vs private scope — what may leave the system | Dual-track is a rule, not a mood. | Pasting raw local output to the public |
| I-9 | Forbidden in public artifacts (PII, secrets, places, brands) | Scrub list is always on. | “We’ll clean it later” |
| I-10 | Codename protocol (yes/no + scheme) | Sensitive entities get stable aliases in durable files. | Real names in committed notes |
| I-11 | First real task (one page, one decision, or one question) | The system is proven on work, not on a tour. | “Explain the whole system to me” |
| I-12 | Review cadence (when you curate and evict notes) | Growth requires eviction, not infinite accumulation. | Never opening the working document again |
| I-13 | Promote rule — what must be true before public ship | Verify blocks ship on OPSEC fail and missing evidence. | Shipping because the chat said “done” |
| I-14 | Non-goals — what this system will not do this season | Scope hygiene keeps the working document readable. | Every interesting idea becomes a skill |

If two builders fill I-1 through I-14 differently, they should get two different systems that still share the kernel. Sameness of brand is not success. Replicability is. Do not print any source-project spine as the framework default. I-2 is written by the new builder, in the new builder’s words.

### TARGET CLASS · pick one per job

- **public-suite** — tools, claims, records, learning path in plain language. Honesty strip on. Operator tokens off HUD.
- **pattern-lab** — experiments, games, visual systems. Fenced. Never contaminates public glass.
- **ops-only** — operator process, session logs, harness work. Not a public product.
- **archive** — finished chapters freeze. Seed left for the next operator.

---

## 02 · Honesty kernel + seven laws + claim scores

Every public claim carries both axes. Missing either axis is a defect. The product UI never auto-mints Supported. Contested claims also carry a tri-state score. The score is not a shortcut around the close rule.

### Two axes (required on every public claim)

| Axis | Values | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| truth_status | Supported | Quote + primary URL. A human closed the cell. Software did not. |
| | Unproven | Plausible, not closed. Hole stays labeled. |
| | Disputed | Records conflict. Show both. Do not average. |
| | Human decision | A person made the share/hold call. Not a substitute for quote + URL. |
| basis | Evidence | Quote / record / data + citation + date. |
| | Inference | Conclusion + one-line reasoning. |
| | Assumption | Unverified premise. Must be flagged. |

### Score mapping · Supported is not identical to +1

The two sources used two scoring dialects. This manual keeps both and forbids collapsing them. **+1** is the score after the close rule. **Supported** is the close rule.

| truth_status | basis required to close | tri-state | Close rule |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Supported | Evidence | +1 only after close | quote + primary URL + human call. Else it is not Supported. |
| Unproven | Evidence, Inference, or Assumption | 0 | Hole stays labeled. Leftover URLs are not quotes. |
| Disputed | Evidence on each side | −1 | Show both records. Do not average. Do not invent a winner. |
| Human decision | states the share/hold | not a score | The release action. Never used to mint Supported. |

### DEFECT

+1 without quote + primary URL + human call is invented Supported. Software emitting “Supported” or auto-assigning +1 is a refuse. Party ticket does not score truth. Influence or percent-control meters are not truth. Empty axes = no extractable row. `mayScore` is false on Lens / Polity Filter.

### Seven laws of the kernel

Write these into `KERNEL.md` in the system’s own words. Domain modules may add procedure. They may not repeal the law.

**Law 1 — Spine before style.**
The system names a mission spine in one sentence (I-2). No spine means Verify has nothing to enforce. A new builder writes their own spine. Copying another operator’s creed is costume.

**Law 2 — Label the claim.**
Every major claim is marked Evidence, Inference, or Assumption. Evidence requires a record, a source, and a date. Inference requires one line of reasoning. Assumption must be flagged as unverified.

**Law 3 — Score the claim.**
Contested claims carry +1 / 0 / −1 after the close rule in the mapping table. Incomplete is allowed. A clean false picture is not.

**Law 4 — Primary records beat commentary.**
Prefer the underlying record over a thread, recap, or pundit layer. A leftover URL is not a quote.

**Law 5 — The working document is mandatory on complex work.**
Decisions, tasks, notes, numbers, verification, and latent state live in a working document with a locked structure. This is how work survives chat reset and handoff.

**Law 6 — Frame audit before synthesis on high-stakes work.**
Frame Audit runs before the system “answers” when Gate 0 is yes (see §6). Answer-first is capture. Polity Filter is a separate civic routing skill (optional packet) and does not replace Frame Audit.

**Law 7 — Human final call; dual track.**
The human releases. Local experiment is free. Public ship is audited. Materials for public use are scrubbed. Raw local work is not a ship.

### GET / REFUSE

| GET | REFUSE |
| --- | --- |
| Quote + primary URL before Supported | Invented Supported / donors / fake sessions |
| Labeled hole when the quote is missing | Influence or % control meters as truth |
| Human final call on every share | Unlabeled mixes of multiple systems |
| Primary record over recap | Leftover URLs treated as quotes |
| Both axes visible on public cards | Software crowning Supported |
| Honest 0 or −1 allowed to stand | +1 without quote + URL + human call |

`honesty-kernel.md` in the seed tree is a one-pager that cites `KERNEL.md`. Do not write two kernels that can drift.

---

## 03 · The building — six floors, five rooms, seven layers

This system is an operating floor for careful thinking. The building has six functions. A **session** is one bounded stretch of work that walks five rooms in order. Skipping Integrity or Coordinate is how private chrome leaks onto public glass.

### Six floors

| Floor | Job | What lives here |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Workshop rules | How work is allowed to run | Charter, refuses, share rules, build modes |
| Knowledge | Sources become linked notes | Vault index, records, wikilinks, provenance |
| Thinking | Tools assist; they do not mint truth | Skills, seats, sessions, honesty labels |
| Public products | Tools + learning path in plain language | Cards, Open Cells, Layer-1 writeups. Globe only if civic packet is on. |
| Private floor | Experiments stay fenced until promoted | Private intake, collector, inbox, operator notes |
| Archive | Finished chapters freeze | Sealed sessions, seeds for the next operator |

### Five rooms · how a session moves

**01 ORIENT**
What question. What domain. What gate. Name the refuse list. Pick the target class. Name the polity only if the civic packet is on.

**02 INTEGRITY**
Honesty labels, conflicts, holes. Nothing is Supported yet unless a prior human call already closed it. On high-stakes work (when Gate 0 is yes), Frame Audit runs here before synthesis.

**03 MISSION**
What must ship this session. One primary artifact. Everything else is optional or next.

**04 COORDINATE**
Who owns which artifact. One artifact, one seat, or an explicit handoff. No freelance past the verb.

**05 SURFACE**
What the public / operator sees. Layer 1 first. Honesty strip on. Operator tokens off HUD.

### Loop on every artifact

Record → Link → Conflict → Human call → Export → Seed. A session that produces no seed is a dead end.

| Step | Does |
| --- | --- |
| RECORD | Capture the primary, the quote, the date, the URL. |
| LINK | Attach it to the card / cell / note. One system id. |
| CONFLICT | If two records disagree, show both. Do not average. |
| HUMAN CALL | A person chooses Supported, hole, or hold. |
| EXPORT | Layer 1 writeup + honesty box + open holes. |
| SEED | Next question, next hole, next owner. Dated. |

### Seven session layers

| Layer | What it holds | Rebuild rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Instructions | Standing laws, refuses, share rules | Write these first. They outrank chat. |
| Agents / seats | Named roles with one verb each | Not a personality dump. Verb + owns + never-owns. |
| Projects | Domain packets with their own memory shards | Plug-in. Keep case files out of the framework pack. |
| Memory | Profile (durable) · log (dated) · note (fades) | Three kinds. Do not mash them into one scrap file. |
| Skills | Reusable playbooks | Verification, reasoning, domain, coordination. Indexed. |
| Modes | How code / visual work is routed | CLOUD default. LOCAL-BOX smoke. LOCAL-HOST rare. |
| Personalization | Operator voice | Never on public glass. Never in the share pack. |

### COMPOSE RULE

A seat may call a skill. A project may hold memory shards. Instructions bind all of them. No seat writes public glass without Verify. No skill mints Supported. No project imports another project’s private material into the framework pack.

---

## 04 · Working document, memory shards, session log

Memory is three timescales, not three competing apps. Do not invent a fourth scrap file.

| Timescale | File | What it is |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PROFILE — durable | `IDENTITY.md` (operator-local) | Who the operator is, standing prefers, standing refuses. Changes rarely. Not a diary. Not in the share pack unless scrubbed of identity. |
| LOG — dated, append-only | `WORKING.md` Decisions / Verification / Growth + `sessions/*.md` | What happened. Decisions, human calls, seeds. Do not silently rewrite history. |
| NOTE — fades | `WORKING.md` Notes | Scratch, hypotheses, half-links. Promote to log or drop. Never ship a note as a claim. |

`vault/index.md` is an OPSEC fence pointer — what must not leave the private floor — not a second working document.

### Locked working-document structure

The working document is the single source of truth for multi-turn work. Load or create it at the start of complex work. Copy it out of the chat into `WORKING.md` before the window dies.

| Cell | Rule | What goes in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Purpose / target class | Set once per job | public-suite \| pattern-lab \| ops-only \| archive, plus one-sentence purpose |
| Decisions | Append-only | Verbatim decision + date. Do not silently rewrite history. |
| Plan tasks | Checkboxes | Work still open, in progress, or evidenced-complete |
| Notes | Curate or evict | Context, open questions. Stale notes get evicted on purpose. |
| Numbers | Named metrics only | Counts, scores, dates, budgets — with units |
| Verification | No self-report | What was checked, by whom (role), what evidence exists |
| Latent state | Handoff packet | Locked decisions, open gaps, correlation ids, current focus |
| Growth log | Required for long work | What was curated, evicted, newly associated |

`WORKING.md` is the live working document. A **session log** (`sessions/S-YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md`) is the dated export of one bounded stretch. Both exist. Do not collapse them. Continuability test: hand the working document and the latest artifact to a second person who was not in the chat. If they cannot continue, the system failed.

---

## 05 · Seats and live roles

Published v3 materials describe 4-agent orchestration. Live practice uses a fixed 3-role model. This manual implements the live model: fewer roles, less theater, same gates. 4-agent text is ancestor.

| Public seat (seed tree) | Live role | Verb | Owns | Never owns |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| coordinate | Coordinator | coordinate | Session order, charter, cross-lane framing, host interface | Day-job spam lanes, case private material |
| build | BUILD / Implement | build | Product artifacts, the named deliverable | Truth minting, self-certify quality |
| verify | VERIFY | gate | First-paint, integrity, P0 leak checklist, ship/no-ship | Feature authorship |
| label | DOMAIN / Label | label | Frame, claim list, card id, kicker, honesty strip. Civic add-on: Track A/B cell labels | Implementation, share decision |

### SEAT NAME LOCK

Charter seats line: `coordinate · build · verify · label`. Folder: `seats/verify.md`. Verb of that seat: **gate**. Do not write `seats/gate.md`. Human / final call is not a seat file. Do not spawn a new seat because a skill exists. Route the skill through the seat that owns the verb. Optional research pods report to coordinator only. Do not grow a live-seat theater on public glass.

Even a solo operator names the role that is speaking and logs the handoff. Simple Q&A stays direct. Complex work declares target class, which roles are on, OPSEC posture, and the next single action. Do not dump three raw walls of role output at the human. Synthesize.

---

## 06 · How work runs

### WHICH CLOCK WHEN

- Every session walks five rooms: Orient → Integrity → Mission → Coordinate → Surface.
- Every artifact walks Gather → Compile → Judge → Do → Check → Gate.
- **Frame Audit default: skip.** Run only when the operator declares Tier 1 / high-stakes, **or** the session touches a claim that could ship (leave Gate).
- **Gate 0** (“Has the operator declared a frame audit?”) **ALWAYS logs yes/no** — even when the answer is no.
- **Gates 1–7 run only when Gate 0 is yes.** Keep all eight gates; depth over ritual; invisible skip is where capture hides.
- Civic plug-in on (I-5 = civic glass): Polity Filter runs after the frame is honest. It does not mint Supported.
- First week: recipe steps 0–8, Table 5 twice, then the dry session.
- If two clocks seem to disagree, the session rooms win for order, Gather→Gate wins for the artifact, and the human wins for share/hold.

### Artifact pipeline

| # | Stage | Does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | GATHER | Primary records, URLs, dates. No commentary first. |
| 2 | COMPILE | Link into cards / cells / notes. One id each. |
| 3 | JUDGE | Label both axes. Surface conflicts. Do not mint. |
| 4 | DO | Build the artifact the mission named. |
| 5 | CHECK | Verify first-paint, leaks, unlabeled mixes. |
| 6 | GATE | Human call. Share or hold. Leave a seed. |

### Skills compose from an index

A skill is a playbook with one verb, a when-clause, steps, refuses, and an output. Skills do not own public glass.

| Skill family | Verb | Owns | Never owns |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Verification | gate | Labels, first-paint, leak checklist, quote+URL rule | Feature authorship, truth minting |
| Reasoning | judge | Conflicts, inferences, assumptions, hole list | Shipping, HUD copy |
| Domain | label | Card id, kicker, honesty strip. Civic add-on: Track A/B cells + axis list | Implementation, share decision |
| Coordination | coordinate | Session order, charter, handoffs, host interface | Day-job spam lanes, case private material |

### Frame Audit · not Polity Filter

**Default: skip Frame Audit.**

Run Frame Audit only when:

1. the operator declares **Tier 1 / high-stakes**, **or**
2. the session touches a claim that could **ship** (leave Gate).

When either condition holds, the operator sets Gate 0 = **yes**. Otherwise Gate 0 = **no**.

- Gate 0 **always** appears in the verification / growth log as yes or no.
- If Gate 0 is **no**, stop. Do not run Gates 1–7. Do not pretend an invisible skip “didn’t happen” — the log line is the proof.
- If Gate 0 is **yes**, run Gates 1–7 before synthesizing. Builders may compose layers. They may not skip this on high-stakes work and call the output finished.

An archived public assumption-audit protocol is the ancestor of Frame Audit (cited once in §14). Polity Filter lives in the civic packet (§8). Do not collapse the two files.

| Gate | Name | Question the system asks |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | Activate | Has the operator declared a frame audit? (Always log yes/no. Default answer: no.) |
| 1 | Token / sensory | What is actually being processed versus what the prompt is steering toward? |
| 2 | Routing / guardrail | What redirection is shaping the output? |
| 3 | Value / accuracy | What accuracy is being deprioritized to avoid refusal or discomfort? |
| 4 | Labeling / hedging | What softening language is weakening the claim? |
| 5 | Composite illusion | Is a unified voice hiding several competing factors? |
| 6 | Evidence Gate | Do remaining claims survive both axes + tri-state? |
| 7 | Close and seal | Are outcomes logged to the working document, including vetoes? |

### Share model

| Layer | When | What it looks like |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Layer 1 — default | Always first | Conversational plain talk. End with an honesty box and open holes — not fake completeness. |
| Layer 2 — on request | Only when asked | Granular depth: scoreboards, seat files, hole lists, quote tables. Do not lead with the machinery. |

---

## 07 · Product surface — cards, cells, optional globe

Every system that ships a public claim needs a card contract and an Open Cells board. A globe host-surface is civic glass. Skip globe rules unless I-5 is civic glass.

### Cards / Claims contract

Every public card has exactly one system id, one public kicker (human label), and an honesty strip (truth status + basis). Unlabeled mixes — multiple systems on one card without separation — are defects. Operator-internal tokens stay in docs, never on HUD.

| Field | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| system_id | One. Stable. Not a sentence. |
| public_kicker | Human label. Plain language. |
| truth_status | Supported / Unproven / Disputed / Human decision |
| basis | Evidence / Inference / Assumption |
| quote | Required to close Supported. Else empty. |
| primary_url | Required to close Supported. Else empty. |
| hole_label | Required if not Supported. |
| notes | Operator only. Never HUD. |

### Open Cells method

- A cell closes Supported only with quote + primary URL + human call.
- Otherwise the cell stays open (labeled hole).
- Leftover URLs are not quotes. Keep `leftover_urls` as a non-closing field.
- No pins for unquoted invent.

### Glass refuses (every public surface)

- × No software auto-crowning Supported.
- × No unlabeled mixes of multiple systems on one card.
- × No leftover URLs treated as quotes.
- × No product-title brand / role-set / seat brand names on public HUD, navigation, or footer (plain language only on glass).
- × No catalog dump on first paint.
- × No iframe of live method hosts into the product.

Civic-only refuses (influence meters, world choropleth of fake scores, Tutor minting Claims scores) live with the civic packet in §8.

---

## 08 · Civic plug-in · optional packet

### SKIP THIS SECTION UNLESS I-5 IS CIVIC GLASS / POWER-MAPPING

A writing system, a QA system, or a research system that is not mapping power does not stand Track A/B boards, a polity-filter skill, scoreboard axes, or globe host-surface rules before the dry session. Those files are the civic plug-in. The floor already has a kernel, seats, working document, cards, Open Cells, Frame Audit, and sessions.

### When the work is civic

- Same scrutiny both ways. Do not go easy on the side you like.
- Challenge before publish. A primary that contradicts you wins.
- Self-correct in the log when a primary contradicts a prior card.
- A hole stays a hole. Do not paint a choropleth over missing quotes.
- Partner country is a variable. Never hard-code one case as the method.

### Polity Filter · a method, not a manifesto on glass

The filter refines routing on civic work after the frame is honest. The honesty kernel still owns Supported. Put this on glass as a method skill, never as a sermon, never as first paint. Desk Layer-0 is the older internal name for this skill only — do not put that name on glass.

| Rule | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Polity gate | Gate on citizen + national sovereignty. The operator names the polity. Do not invent one. |
| Foreign entanglement | In scope when it hardens into national policy. Not in scope as vibes or headlines. |
| Partner variable | Partner country is a variable. Never hard-code one case as the method. |
| Scoreboard axes | Templates only. Empty until a primary fills a cell. No invented winners. |
| Kernel still owns | The filter does not mint Supported. Honesty kernel + human call do. |

Scoreboard axis list (empty templates — keep the list, do not fill winners in the framework pack): companies · countries · industries · individuals · chambers · named committees · regulators · education · research · civil society (separate) · capital paths.

### Track A / Track B · civic speech is not library attach

When mapping power, keep two tracks structurally separate. Collapsing them is how a method becomes a story. This is not library attach. GitHub ZIPs are never called Track B.

| Track | Definition | Typical records |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A — contracts | Partnership / procurement / R&D / funding authorities that produce contracts, grants, access, co-production | Awards, solicitations, cooperative agreements, grant notices, docketed procurements |
| B — speech / definitions | Speech / definitional / platform / campus law and interpretation governed elsewhere | Statutes, guidance, Terms, civil-rights letters, AG civil actions, duty-of-care bills, assessment statutes |

### LINK RULE

Track B can constrain who performs Track A contracts (and how). Track A can raise stakes around Track B actors. Close a cross-link cell only with a primary that ties them.

### Globe host-surface (only if I-5 is civic glass)

| Rule | Do | Do not |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Mount | Globe stays the host surface. | Replace the globe with a catalog dump on first paint. |
| Freeze | Freeze camera. No auto-fly / auto-zoom while frozen. | Steal the camera when a layer toggles. |
| Layers | Multi layers / tabs may stay open together. | Let a toggle unfreeze or yank selection. |
| Select | Selection marks the globe without flying when frozen. | Fly-to on every click. |
| Work | Desks, drawers, scenario tools sit over the frozen globe. | Navigate by flying the user around. |

### Civic glass refuses (add to the floor refuses when the packet is on)

- × No influence meter dressed as civic truth.
- × No world choropleth of fake scores · pins for unquoted invent.
- × No Tutor / lesson engine minting Claims scores.
- × Collapsing Track A and Track B without a primary.
- × Treating unenacted bill text as executed law.

---

## 09 · Build modes, two-layer seed tree, library attach

### How code moves

| Mode | Use | Rebuild rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| CLOUD | Default for repository code — branch + PR; operator merges | Open PRs ready for review (undrafted) and mergeable. |
| LOCAL-BOX | Visual smoke on the assistant computer after the operator has seen once | Smoke only. Local pixels are not the source of truth. |
| LOCAL-HOST | Only when the operator machine filesystem / login is required | Rare. Coordinator picks this. Do not ask the operator to swap tools. |
| Optional third | Off unless the operator explicitly re-enables | Default off. Do not quietly turn it on. |

Coordinator picks the mode. Host layout is not assumed. No-repo path is primary. A folder the builder controls plus a new model session is enough to start.

### Seed tree · two layers

A rebuilder with no root repos starts here. Empty templates. No winners. No private-floor dumps. Floor files are required for every system. Civic plug-in files are created only when I-5 is civic glass.

#### Floor (required)

```
base/
  IDENTITY.md                       operator-local identity (do not share filled)
  KERNEL.md                         seven laws in the system's words
  WORKING.md                        live working document
  charter.md                        shareable standing law
  honesty-kernel.md                 two axes + close rule (cites KERNEL.md)
  refuses.md
  share-model.md
  build-modes.md
  seats/coordinate.md
  seats/build.md
  seats/verify.md                   file name = verify; verb = gate
  seats/label.md                    frame + claim list + honesty strip
  skills/index.md
  skills/verification.md
  skills/reasoning.md
  skills/domain.md
  skills/coordination.md
  skills/frame-audit.md             Frame Audit — do not name this desk-layer-0
  contracts/cards.md
  contracts/open-cells.md
  contracts/phase-gates.md
  vault/index.md                    OPSEC fence — not a second working document
  sessions/_template.md
  sessions/_dry-session.md
  archive/.keep
```

#### Civic plug-in (create only if I-5 = civic glass)

```
  skills/polity-filter.md           Desk-0 / Polity Filter — do not collapse with Frame Audit
  contracts/track-a-b.md
  scoreboards/axes.md               empty names only
  product/globe-rules.md
  product/glass-refuses.md
```

**File-name note:** older architecture text used `skills/desk-layer-0.md`. This manual splits that name so Frame Audit and Polity Filter cannot be collapsed by a filename.

### Library attach (optional) — after Table 5

This is not civic Track B. Civic Track B is speech / definitions (§8). Library attach is an optional published-tree add-on after the kernel stands. Two public trees exist in the source record. Both cited trees were archived on or before this manual’s sources were frozen. They are optional attach-after, not the implement path.

Keep `KERNEL.md` and `WORKING.md` as law. Published skills do not outrank them. Attach only core / public protocols until session one has passed Table 5. Translate remaining “4-Agent” text to BUILD / VERIFY / DOMAIN. Do not attach specialized security-operator folders unless the system’s lawful scope is authorized security process design. This manual does not teach exploitation. Full URLs live in the citation leaf (§14).

---

## 10 · Rebuild recipe · one path

Do not plug a real domain until step 8 is done. Coordinator picks modes. Operator merges. The three-week calendar is the wrapping schedule, not a competing recipe. First-session A–F is the no-repo expansion of steps 0–2 and 8, not a second clock.

| Step | Do | Done when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | Fill I-1–I-14 in `IDENTITY.md`. | No blanks on I-2, I-3, I-9, I-11. Human signed the declaration line. |
| 1 | Write `KERNEL.md` + `charter.md` + `refuses.md` + `honesty-kernel.md`. | Four files exist. Human signed the human-final-call line on the charter. |
| 2 | Stand four seats: coordinate · build · verify · label. Open `WORKING.md` with Purpose filled. | Each seat file has verb, owns, never-owns, reports-to. Working document exists outside the chat. |
| 3 | Define card contract + Open Cells template. | Blank board with the quote+URL rule printed on it. |
| 4 | Mount a globe with freeze + multi-layer rules. | Skip if I-5 is not civic glass. Else: frozen camera; toggles do not steal it. |
| 5 | Pick CLOUD for code; LOCAL visual only for smoke. | PRs undrafted and mergeable when a repo exists. No tool-swap requests. |
| 6 | Add Polity Filter as a method skill. | Skip unless I-5 is civic glass. Else: skill file exists; no manifesto on first paint. |
| 7 | Add Track A / Track B separation before any hot case. | Skip unless I-5 is civic glass. Else: two empty boards; cross-link cells exist and are open. |
| 8 | Run session-one (Table 5) then one dry session on a toy domain. | Table 5 all 8 rows Yes. Drill objects exist. Seed left. Case files still empty. |
| 9 | Only then plug a real domain. Keep case files out of the framework pack. | Domain packet has its own memory shards. Framework pack still clean. |
| 10 | Archive finished chapters; leave seeds. | Archive folder has a frozen session + a dated seed. |

### Three-week wrapping calendar

| When | Build | Done when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Week 1 — Kernel | Steps 0–3 and 5. Five real tasks through the paste block. | Table 5 passes twice. Growth log has at least one eviction. |
| Week 2 — Three cells | Three short modules in the system’s voice: claim scorer, frame audit helper, coordinator. | Each module has purpose, triggers, never-do list, output shape. One task used all three. |
| Week 3 — One domain desk | Steps 9–10. One module for I-5 only. | A continuable artifact exists. Verify logged OPSEC on it. |
| Ongoing — Growth | Curate notes, evict stale cells, record new associations, review I-12 cadence. | Working document stays readable by a stranger. Skill count is not the score. |

Catalog tourism is not a week. Installing the published skill zoo before Table 5 is a fail.

### No-repo expansion of steps 0–2 and 8

1. **A.** Fill I-1–I-14. Stop if I-2 or I-11 is blank.
2. **B.** Create a folder the builder controls. Put `IDENTITY.md`, `KERNEL.md`, `WORKING.md` in it.
3. **C.** Open a new model session. Paste Template C (§13.12) with bracketed fields replaced. Attach `KERNEL.md` and `WORKING.md` only.
4. **D.** First model output must include a filled Purpose cell and at least one Plan task. Reject the turn if it does not.
5. **E.** DOMAIN lists claims. BUILD produces the artifact. VERIFY writes a verification cell. Human accepts, rejects, or sends back.
6. **F.** Copy the updated working document out of the chat into `WORKING.md`. If the host forgets tomorrow, the system still exists.

---

## 11 · Dual-track OPSEC, hard refuses, failure modes

A refuse is a stop, not a style note. If a session wants one of these, hold and write the hole. Local experiment is free. Public ship is audited. Promotion is a session, not a copy-paste.

### Always-on scrub list

- No legal names, phones, emails, home addresses, or account identifiers in samples.
- No secrets: API keys, tokens, cookies, private keys, `.env` values.
- No municipality names in samples, packs, or shareable demos (geographic agnosticism).
- No internal tool paths or host topology.
- No raw working documents or chat exports.
- No operator skill brands or live-seat chrome in public product UI, navigation, or footers.
- No promote of raw scrapes. Quarantine stays quarantine until Verify and the human say otherwise.
- No filled `IDENTITY.md` in the share pack. No filled scoreboard winners inside the framework pack.

### Hard refuses (floor)

- × Invent Supported · invent donors · invent sessions · invent dollar schedules
- × Catalog dump on first paint · iframe method hosts
- × Mixing private-floor / collector / inbox chrome into public glass
- × Shipping operator brain paths, emails, mail links, or private keys
- × Unlabeled mixes (multiple systems on one card without separation)
- × Leftover URLs treated as quotes
- × Software auto-crowning Supported
- × Calling +1 “Supported” without quote + URL + human call
- × Product ceremonial names / live-seat labels on public HUD
- × Collapsing Frame Audit with Polity Filter

### Add when the civic packet is on

- × Influence / “% foreign control” meters as truth
- × Collapsing Track A and Track B without a primary
- × Treating unenacted bill text as executed law
- × World choropleth of fake scores · pins for unquoted invent
- × Tutor / lesson engine minting Claims scores
- × Party ticket used as a truth score
- × Hard-coding one partner country as the method
- × Filling scoreboard winners inside the framework pack

### May share / must strip

**May share:** charter, kernel, refuses, templates; empty axes, empty cells, empty seats; Layer 1 writeups with honesty boxes; this manual; blank individualization sheet.

**Must strip:** private case files and private-floor dumps; inbox / collector / operator brain paths; keys, mail links, emails, host filesystem; filled winners and municipality samples; filled `IDENTITY.md` identity answers.

### Failure modes

| Anti-pattern | What it looks like | Correction |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Catalog tourism | Fifty skills attached, zero working-document lines | Delete attachments. Pass Table 5 first. |
| Costume spine | Pasted another operator’s creed | Rewrite I-2 in the builder’s words or halt. |
| Answer-first | Long synthesis, audit promised “later” | Restart the turn at Frame Audit Gate 0. |
| Self-report ship | “Done,” “tests passed,” no artifact | Verify rejects until the file exists. |
| False complete picture | Every claim scored +1 from one blog | Mark 0 or −1. Primary records or silence. |
| Chrome leak | Ceremonial / role-set names on a public civic screen | Rewrite public copy in plain language. |
| Infinite notes | Notes never evicted; working document unreadable | Forced curation session. Growth-log the evictions. |
| Host superstition | “It only works on this machine / this path” | Re-run from a folder + new chat. Platform is portable. |
| Layer collapse | Frame Audit used as a polity sermon, or Polity Filter used as a prompt audit | Keep Frame Audit and Polity Filter in separate files. |
| Score laundering | “Supported because +1” with no quote | Re-open the cell. Apply §2 mapping. |
| Civic bolted to floor | Writing system forced to stand Track A/B before a dry session | Skip steps 4, 6, 7 unless I-5 is civic glass. |

---

## 12 · Pass / fail audits

Charming chat does not substitute. A system with all +1 scores and no artifacts is still a −1 on continuability.

### Table 5 · session-one (Gate S)

| Session-one test | Pass |
| --- | --- |
| `IDENTITY.md` has I-1–I-14 | Yes / No |
| `KERNEL.md` states seven laws in the system’s voice | Yes / No |
| `WORKING.md` exists outside the chat | Yes / No |
| At least one Decision line with a date | Yes / No |
| At least one claim labeled E/I/A | Yes / No |
| At least one 0 or −1 was allowed to stand | Yes / No |
| Verification cell is not “looks good” | Yes / No |
| A second person could continue from the files | Yes / No |

Gate S requires all eight rows Yes. The continuability row is not optional.

### Phase gate list · rebuild (Gate P)

- ☐ charter + honesty kernel + refuses exist
- ☐ four seats stood (coordinate / build / verify / label)
- ☐ every public card has id · kicker · strip
- ☐ every cell is quote+URL or labeled hole
- ☐ verify: first-paint, no P0 leak, no mix
- ☐ human call recorded in the session log
- ☐ Layer 1 export + holes · seed left
- ☐ `IDENTITY.md` not included filled in the share pack
- ☐ dry session logged on a toy domain
- ☐ Frame Audit skill file exists
- ☐ Frame Audit Gate 0 yes/no line is present in at least one verification or growth log
- ☐ when I-5 is civic glass: Track A / Track B not collapsed
- ☐ when I-5 is civic glass: Polity Filter applied (polity named by the operator)
- ☐ when I-5 is civic glass: globe freeze + multi-layer rules written
- ☐ when I-5 is civic glass: empty scoreboard axis list (names present, winners absent)

### Table 7 · implementation audit (week 1 and week 3)

| Claim about the new system | Score | Evidence required |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A written spine exists and is used | +1 / 0 / −1 | I-2 text + one logged spine check |
| Claims are labeled and scored | +1 / 0 / −1 | Three examples in `WORKING.md` |
| State survives a new chat | +1 / 0 / −1 | `WORKING.md` opened in a fresh session, work continued |
| High-stakes work hits Frame Audit first (Gate 0=yes then 1–7) | +1 / 0 / −1 | One sealed Gate 0–7 note; or Gate 0=no logged when work was not high-stakes |
| Verify rejected at least one self-report | +1 / 0 / −1 | Verification cell that sent work back |
| Public-facing text was scrubbed | +1 / 0 / −1 | Before/after or a written promote decision |
| A stranger can continue | +1 / 0 / −1 | Independent read of IDENTITY + KERNEL + WORKING + artifact |

### Dry session · rooms walk (objects live in §13)

**QUESTION · Does this public trail-map legend list winter hours?**

- **Orient:** domain = recreation posting. Gate = public-share. No polity — this is not civic glass.
- **Integrity:** do not invent hours. No pin until a quote exists. Both axes required. Nothing Supported. Gate 0 = no (not Tier 1; claim not shipping yet) — log the no.
- **Mission:** one card + one Open Cell + five `WORKING.md` lines. Layer 1 sentence.
- **Coordinate:** Label owns the card. Verify owns the gate. Coordinator owns the seed.
- **Surface:** “Winter hours are not posted on the legend we have.” Honesty: Unproven / Assumption, hole labeled.

Hours on a legend is a posting record. Civic Track B is speech/definitions. The drill does not borrow that letter.

---

## 13 · Copy-paste templates + DRILL ONLY objects

One schema set. Do not invent a second. Copy these into files. Do not fill winners. Do not paste private case content.

### 13.1 IDENTITY.md · blank individualization sheet (operator-local)

```yaml
# IDENTITY.md
# Older packs used COLONY.md — treat as alias of this file.
system_name:                       # I-1
mission_spine:                     # I-2 one sentence you will not bargain
final_call_rule:                   # I-3 who has final call, on what
default_target_class:              # I-4 public-suite | pattern-lab | ops-only | archive
first_domain:                      # I-5
host_and_session_start:            # I-6
memory_substrate:                  # I-7
shared_vs_private:                 # I-8
forbidden_in_public:               # I-9
codename_protocol:                 # I-10
first_real_task:                   # I-11
review_cadence:                    # I-12
promote_rule:                      # I-13
non_goals_this_season:             # I-14

declaration: I will not paste private case content, secrets, or another person's PII into this system's public track.
human_initials_date:
```

### 13.2 charter.md · shareable standing law

```yaml
# charter.md
purpose: operating floor for careful thinking
success: another careful person rebuilds the base, then plugs their own domain
refuses: invent Supported / donors / sessions / dollar schedules
          catalog dump on first paint
          iframe live method hosts
          mix private-floor material onto glass
          leftover URLs treated as quotes
          software crowning Supported
          ceremonial / live-seat names on public HUD
          collapse Frame Audit and Polity Filter
seats:    coordinate · build · verify · label
share:    Layer 1 default · Layer 2 on request
human_final_call: yes
signed:
```

### 13.3 Honesty kernel one-pager

| Field | Write this |
| --- | --- |
| Axes | truth_status: Supported \| Unproven \| Disputed \| Human decision; basis: Evidence \| Inference \| Assumption |
| Close rule | Supported only with quote + primary URL + human call |
| Open rule | Else labeled hole. Leftover URLs are not quotes. |
| Score rule | +1 only after close. Unproven = 0. Disputed = −1. +1 without close is a defect. |
| Laws | Primary records > commentary. Incomplete > fake-complete. No invented sessions/donors/dollars. |
| UI | Product never auto-mints Supported. Honesty strip on every public card. |

### 13.4 KERNEL.md

Copy the seven law titles from §2. Rewrite each body sentence in the system’s words. Do not paste another operator’s creed into Law 1. Law 1 is I-2.

### 13.5 WORKING.md · working document

```markdown
# WORKING — [system name] — [job title]
# Older packs used COMB.md — treat as alias of this file.

## Purpose / target class
Target class:
Purpose (one sentence):

## Decisions (append-only)
- [YYYY-MM-DD]

## Plan tasks
- [ ]

## Notes

## Numbers

## Verification
- Check:
- Evidence:
- Tri-state on the main claim:
- Frame Audit Gate 0: yes | no
- Promote readiness: no | quarantine | yes (human only)

## Latent state
- Locked decisions:
- Open gaps:
- Current focus:

## Growth log
- Curated:
- Evicted:
- New association:
```

### 13.6 Seat file

```yaml
seat:                 <name>
verb:                 <one verb>
owns:                 <artifact classes>
never_owns:           <explicit>
reports_to:           coordinator
handoff_when:         <what must be true to pass the artifact>

# Minimum four
seat: coordinator   verb: coordinate
owns: session order, charter, handoffs, host interface
never_owns: day-job spam lanes, case private material

seat: build         verb: build
owns: product artifacts, the named deliverable
never_owns: truth minting, self-certify

seat: verify        verb: gate
owns: first-paint, integrity, P0 leak checklist
never_owns: feature authorship
# file name = seats/verify.md   do not write seats/gate.md

seat: label         verb: label
owns: frame, claim list, card id, kicker, honesty strip
never_owns: implementation, share decision
# civic add-on when packet is on: Track A/B cell labels
```

### 13.7 Open Cell · blank row

```yaml
cell_id:              C-<track-or-toy>-<nnn>
question:             <one question>
track:                A | B | cross | n/a
quote:                <verbatim or empty>
primary_url:          <url or empty>
status:               open | supported
truth_status:         Unproven | Supported | Disputed | Human decision
basis:                Evidence | Inference | Assumption
hole_label:           <required if not supported>
leftover_urls:        <do not close on these>
closed_by:            <human, date, or empty>
seed_next:            <next question or empty>
```

### 13.8 Session log

```yaml
session_id:           S-YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>
date:
question:
domain:               <plug-in name, not case chrome>
gate:                 public-share | private-floor | archive
rooms_run:            orient · integrity · mission · coordinate · surface
frame_audit_gate_0:   yes | no
artifacts:            <paths or ids>
conflicts:            <or none>
human_call:           <Supported / hole / hold>
export:               Layer 1 + honesty box + holes
seed_next:            <dated, owned>
```

### 13.9 Skill / module file · one verb

```yaml
name: [short-name]
status: draft | active | absorbed
target_class: ops-only | public-suite | pattern-lab | archive
verb: <one>
when: <activate clause>
reports_through: <seat verb, not a new seat>
steps: Gather → Compile → Judge → Do → Check → Gate
never: <OPSEC, auto-truth, scope>
verification: evidence that this module ran. Self-report is insufficient.
```

### 13.10 Frame-audit skill stub (floor)

```yaml
name:            frame-audit
verb:            audit
when:            operator declares Tier 1 / high-stakes; OR session touches a claim that could ship (leave Gate). Default: skip.
reports_through: verify
steps:           0 Activate (ALWAYS log yes/no) · if yes then:
                 1 Token/sensory · 2 Routing/guardrail
                 3 Value/accuracy · 4 Labeling/hedging · 5 Composite illusion
                 6 Evidence Gate · 7 Close and seal
never:           mint Supported; skip on high-stakes and call the output finished;
                 run Gates 1–7 when Gate 0 is no; collapse with Polity Filter;
                 leave Gate 0 unlogged
outputs:         sealed Gate 0 (always) and Gates 1–7 (when Gate 0=yes) note in WORKING Verification + Growth log, including vetoes
```

### 13.11 Polity-filter skill stub (civic plug-in only)

```yaml
name:            polity-filter
verb:            filter
when:            civic work after the frame is honest; operator has named a polity
reports_through: label
steps:           name polity
                 test foreign entanglement only when it hardens into national policy
                 keep partner country a variable
                 keep scoreboard axes empty until a primary fills a cell
                 do not mint Supported
never:           manifesto on first paint; invent a polity;
                 hard-code one partner as the method; fill winners in the framework pack
```

### 13.12 First-session paste block

Operator-session text. Not public product UI copy. Replace bracketed fields from `IDENTITY.md`.

```text
You are running a small evidence-first operating harness for [SYSTEM NAME].

Mission spine: [I-2]
Human final call: [I-3]
Default target class: [I-4]
Forbidden in shareable output: [I-9]

Rules:
- Label every major claim Evidence / Inference / Assumption.
- Score contested claims +1 / 0 / -1 after the close rule, and say why.
- Supported requires quote + primary URL + human call. Software never crowns it.
- Prefer primary records over commentary.
- Prefer honest incomplete state over a clean false picture.
- Keep a working document with: Purpose, Decisions, Plan, Notes,
  Numbers, Verification, Latent state, Growth log.
- Frame Audit default: skip. Run only when Tier 1 / high-stakes is declared,
  or a claim could ship. Always log Gate 0 yes/no. Gates 1–7 only if Gate 0 is yes.
- Do not put ceremonial role-set names into public product UI copy.

Roles even if you are one model:
- DOMAIN frames the problem, lists claims, and owns card id / kicker / honesty strip.
- BUILD makes the artifact.
- VERIFY gates quality, scrubbing, and completion evidence.

Synthesize. Do not dump three raw role walls.
Start WORKING.md in this reply. Then do this task:
[I-11]
```

### 13.13 DRILL ONLY — three filled objects

**DRILL ONLY**
Toy domain: recreation posting. Not a case file. Not a product sample. Do not keep these filled objects in a share pack as evidence of anything except “the method produced a file.”

#### Object 1 — one card

```yaml
system_id:     trail-legend-hours
public_kicker: Winter hours on the trail-map legend
truth_status: Unproven
basis:         Assumption
quote:
primary_url:
hole_label:    Current legend we have does not state winter hours
notes:         (operator only — never HUD)
```

#### Object 2 — one Open Cell

